WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.819 --> 00:00:18.481
Jonathan searched for Marissa as soon as he arrived at the soccer field Saturday afternoon.

2
00:00:19.282 --> 00:00:20.642
He spotted her on the sideline.

3
00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:25.185
"I'm going to walk Pastrami down the sideline to get his energy out," he said to his parents.

4
00:00:25.205 --> 00:00:27.446
"Energy?" Mr.

5
00:00:27.466 --> 00:00:28.006
Cho echoed.

6
00:00:28.026 --> 00:00:30.568
"In this heat even the dog has no energy."

7
00:00:31.596 --> 00:00:34.697
Pastrami lay on the grass, looking as energetic as an old tortoise.

8
00:00:34.717 --> 00:00:38.839
"I think he really wants to go for a walk," Jonathan said quickly.

9
00:00:38.859 --> 00:00:42.000
"Aren't you supposed to start warming up with your team?"

10
00:00:42.581 --> 00:00:43.201
asked his mom.

11
00:00:44.361 --> 00:00:48.143
Jonathan ignored her, yanking on Pastrami's leash as they trudged down the sideline.

12
00:00:52.425 --> 00:00:53.885
They passed Carlos and his family.

13
00:00:54.606 --> 00:00:59.808
His mother fanned herself and called to Jonathan, "Oh, this horrible weather!

14
00:01:00.684 --> 00:01:02.745
How will you and my baby Carlos run in this heat?"

15
00:01:03.866 --> 00:01:04.726
"We'll be fine, Mrs.

16
00:01:04.786 --> 00:01:06.327
Ruiz!" Jonathan laughed.

17
00:01:07.168 --> 00:01:11.030
Mrs. Cho called Jonathan Johnnyboy, but at least she never called him a baby!

18
00:01:14.652 --> 00:01:19.134
Jonathan walked over to Marissa, who looked especially cute today in a bright red sundress and a high

19
00:01:19.174 --> 00:01:22.476
ponytail. He had to get this apology over with.

20
00:01:23.517 --> 00:01:25.858
Jonathan waved at her awkwardly, but she turned away.

21
00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:28.640
Pastrami yapped and wagged his tail.

22
00:01:30.568 --> 00:01:32.049
Still Marissa kept her back to them.

23
00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:38.353
Jonathan quickly started walking Pastrami farther down the sideline, pretending that he'd just been walking the dog.

24
00:01:41.995 --> 00:01:44.156
Marissa obviously wanted nothing to do with Jonathan.

25
00:01:44.876 --> 00:01:48.678
Though she probably would have loved seeing Pastrami again if Jonathan weren't holding his leash.

26
00:01:49.819 --> 00:01:54.402
Back at his parents' chairs, Jonathan gave Pastrami a drink and then splashed some water on his own

27
00:01:54.462 --> 00:02:00.961
face. He was really hot—and his embarrassment over Marissa wasn't helping one bit.

28
00:02:02.202 --> 00:02:04.423
After warm-up drills Jonathan felt even hotter.

29
00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:08.105
Sweat dripped from his forehead as he walked to the center of the field.

30
00:02:10.947 --> 00:02:16.170
Today his team was playing the Silver Bombers, another name that sounded a million times cooler than Team

31
00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:23.194
Wattenbarger. The Silver Bombers had three substitutes—three more than Jonathan's team had, now that Andrew and Aaron had

32
00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:23.794
quit the team.

33
00:02:26.395 --> 00:02:27.176
The game began.

34
00:02:27.892 --> 00:02:30.955
Jonathan panted as he chased the ball up and down the hot field.

35
00:02:34.518 --> 00:02:36.660
He wished Andrew and Aaron had stayed on the team.

36
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.861
He wished he had a different coach.

37
00:02:39.662 --> 00:02:41.323
He wished Max would share the ball.

38
00:02:42.144 --> 00:02:43.786
He wished Marissa would wave back at him.

39
00:02:44.686 --> 00:02:46.067
He wished it were cooler outside.

40
00:02:46.728 --> 00:02:49.771
He wished— "Jonathan, pay attention!"

41
00:02:50.511 --> 00:02:52.993
Coach Wattenbarger barked as the ball sailed toward him.

42
00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:56.016
Jonathan trapped the ball and glanced at the goal.

43
00:02:59.148 --> 00:03:02.111
He wasn't very close, but he might be able to shoot the ball in.

44
00:03:02.131 --> 00:03:04.212
"Pass it to Max!"

45
00:03:04.693 --> 00:03:05.513
the coach screamed.

46
00:03:06.354 --> 00:03:10.477
Max was double-teamed by the Silver Bombers, but Jonathan kicked the ball to him anyway.

47
00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.262
A Silver Bomber got it and made a long, high pass to a teammate.

48
00:03:17.043 --> 00:03:20.206
That guy headed the ball to another teammate, who passed it to another teammate.

49
00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.732
The Silver Bombers kept passing the ball up the field.

50
00:03:28.876 --> 00:03:30.136
"They work so well together.

51
00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.237
No ball hogs on their team!"

52
00:03:33.037 --> 00:03:34.878
Jonathan thought as he ran to defend the ball.

53
00:03:35.738 --> 00:03:36.538
But it was useless.

54
00:03:37.299 --> 00:03:40.540
Thanks to their excellent passing, the Silver Bombers scored a goal.

55
00:03:45.781 --> 00:03:47.001
Coach Wattenbarger yelled.

56
00:03:47.642 --> 00:03:49.482
Jonathan kicked the grass in frustration.

57
00:03:50.983 --> 00:03:52.723
Max stood next to him at the kickoff.

58
00:03:52.743 --> 00:03:55.104
"Sorry I missed your pass, Jonathan."

59
00:03:56.268 --> 00:04:00.010
"You were double-teamed, but your dad still made me pass to you," Jonathan grumbled.

60
00:04:00.811 --> 00:04:01.771
Max didn't respond.

61
00:04:03.212 --> 00:04:07.555
The game continued with three substitute Silver Bombers and no substitute Wattenbargers.

62
00:04:08.295 --> 00:04:10.276
Team Wattenbarger kept passing Max the ball.

63
00:04:13.698 --> 00:04:18.321
But with the Silver Bombers double-teaming him, he kept losing the ball, and his father kept yelling at

64
00:04:18.361 --> 00:04:23.464
him. Jonathan was grateful to hear the referee's whistle announce halftime.

65
00:04:24.148 --> 00:04:26.930
The team, dripping with sweat, staggered off the field.

66
00:04:31.032 --> 00:04:35.315
miserable. I should quit the team like the twins did," Jonathan moaned.

67
00:04:36.155 --> 00:04:37.116
Carlos shook his head.

68
00:04:37.136 --> 00:04:38.657
"You can't quit.

69
00:04:39.277 --> 00:04:39.958
We need you."

70
00:04:39.978 --> 00:04:42.819
"You don't need me to watch Max hog the ball.

71
00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.121
I know he's the best player in the league."

72
00:04:45.981 --> 00:04:47.022
Jonathan rolled his eyes.

73
00:04:47.042 --> 00:04:51.952
"But even Max can't score when he's double-teamed."

74
00:04:51.972 --> 00:04:54.134
Carlos shot a look at the coach and then lowered his voice.

75
00:04:54.154 --> 00:04:56.756
"You and I know how to play soccer together.

76
00:04:57.657 --> 00:05:01.520
The next time Max is double-teamed, I'll pass you the ball, and you can take a shot at

77
00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:01.920
the goal."

78
00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.983
"Coach would get mad," Jonathan said.

79
00:05:05.623 --> 00:05:06.364
Carlos shrugged.

80
00:05:06.964 --> 00:05:08.425
"He won't be mad if you score a goal."

81
00:05:08.445 --> 00:05:11.708
"He might still be mad," Jonathan said.

82
00:05:11.728 --> 00:05:14.851
"But you know what—that's a great idea, Carlos.

83
00:05:15.591 --> 00:05:16.852
Let's try it in the second half!"

84
00:05:17.873 --> 00:05:21.396
At the halftime meeting, Coach Wattenbarger folded his arms across his chest.

85
00:05:22.728 --> 00:05:24.850
"Max, you played horribly today."

86
00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.493
"I was double-teamed most of the time," Max muttered.

87
00:05:28.513 --> 00:05:30.815
"Stop making excuses!

88
00:05:31.635 --> 00:05:33.477
You'll never get a college scholarship that way."

89
00:05:34.478 --> 00:05:37.040
Jonathan pitied Max even more than he pitied himself.

90
00:05:37.961 --> 00:05:39.702
Max's father was so hard on Max.

91
00:05:40.643 --> 00:05:45.387
During the second half, Team Wattenbarger panted and sweated while the Silver Bombers substituted players.

92
00:05:46.428 --> 00:05:49.610
Max tried hard to score, but he was constantly double-teamed.

93
00:05:50.471 --> 00:05:52.753
Once Carlos got the ball, he kicked it to Jonathan.

94
00:05:56.916 --> 00:05:57.776
Pass to Max!"

95
00:05:58.317 --> 00:05:59.017
the coach yelled.

96
00:05:59.998 --> 00:06:04.641
Jonathan glanced at Max, who had two Silver Bombers drawn to him like magnets.

97
00:06:05.542 --> 00:06:08.784
Instead of passing, Jonathan took a long shot toward the goal.

98
00:06:08.804 --> 00:06:12.606
"Go, Johnnyboy!"

99
00:06:12.887 --> 00:06:14.288
his mother yelled from the sideline.

100
00:06:15.048 --> 00:06:15.969
Jonathan cringed.

101
00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:20.532
The Silver Bomber goalie caught the ball and kicked it hard down the field.

102
00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.961
His teammate headed it to another teammate, who headed it to one of their forwards.

103
00:06:28.941 --> 00:06:33.283
The forward trapped it, dribbled it, and then kicked it right into the Wattenbargers' goal.

104
00:06:37.744 --> 00:06:38.984
play, Carlos and Jonathan!"

105
00:06:39.464 --> 00:06:40.284
the coach bellowed.

106
00:06:41.125 --> 00:06:42.425
Jonathan's stomach sank.

107
00:06:43.305 --> 00:06:44.446
It sure was a bad play.

108
00:06:46.846 --> 00:06:49.747
Jonathan felt nothing but relief when the game ended a few minutes later.

109
00:06:50.427 --> 00:06:54.060
The Wattenbargers had lost, 0–2.

110
00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.162
As he walked off the field, Jonathan apologized to Carlos.

111
00:06:59.904 --> 00:07:00.984
"Sorry I missed that shot."

112
00:07:01.004 --> 00:07:03.926
"It was my idea," Carlos said.

113
00:07:05.487 --> 00:07:06.928
The coach called the team over to him.

114
00:07:07.588 --> 00:07:12.311
He leaned forward, giving Jonathan a close-up view of his angry red face and big bald head.

115
00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.572
"You boys were terrible today!

116
00:07:15.292 --> 00:07:17.234
And, Max, you need more practice.

117
00:07:18.014 --> 00:07:19.455
No video games for you this week."

118
00:07:20.435 --> 00:07:21.216
Max hung his head.

119
00:07:22.064 --> 00:07:23.946
After the team meeting, Jonathan went over to Max.

120
00:07:23.966 --> 00:07:28.049
"Your dad needs to give you a break.

121
00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:31.712
It wasn't your fault that you were double-teamed and we had no substitutes."

122
00:07:32.873 --> 00:07:34.634
Max looked surprised—and grateful.

123
00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:37.056
"Thanks, Jonathan," he said.

124
00:07:37.076 --> 00:07:38.878
"I'm glad you're on my team."

125
00:07:39.838 --> 00:07:43.181
"Me too," Jonathan said, surprised to realize that he meant it.

126
00:07:44.182 --> 00:07:45.663
He just wished they had a different coach.
